{
  "title": "Blood Supply to the Foot",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/12114/blood-supply-to-the-foot",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 7 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Source Arteries",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Blood supply of foot comes from three primary source arteries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Peroneal (fibular) artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Posterior tibial artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Anterior tibial artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Peroneal (Fibular) Artery",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Origin",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arises from **the posterior tibial artery** approximately 2.5 cm from its origin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/fig_5.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/origin_back_knee.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Course in leg",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pierces interosseous membrane ~ 5 cm above lateral malleolus as perforating branch and communicates with the **anterior lateral malleolar artery**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "then passes down anterior to tibiofibular syndesmosis to anastomose with **lateral tarsal artery**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "supplies the soleus, tibialis posterior, flexor hallicus longus, and peroneal muscles along its course",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Branches at ankle",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**posterior lateral malleolar artery**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**communicating branch**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Branches in foot",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**lateral calcaneal branch**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "terminal branch of the peroneal artery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "provides perfusion to the lateral flap associated with a standard extensile approach to the calcaneus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/fig10.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Posterior Tibial Artery",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Origin**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "largest of the two terminal branches of the popliteal artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/fig_5.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "its most proximal part is referred to as the tibioperoneal trunk",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Course in leg**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "it passes between the superficial and deep muscles of the posterior compartment of the lower leg",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "as it courses down the lower leg it becomes more medial and is palpable behind the medial malleolus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Branches at the ankle**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**posterior medial malleolar artery**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**communicating branch**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**artery of tarsal canal**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**dominant blood supply to the talar body**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Branches in foot**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**beneath sustentaculum posterior tibial artery bifurcates into**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral plantar arteries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "branches",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**medial calcaneal branch (first branch)**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/fig_3.jpg",
                              "caption": ""
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "is the major vascular supply to the heel pad",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "text": "heel pad avulsions are severe injuries associated with high-energy trauma and often carry a poor prognosis because of the potential for heel pad necrosis",
                                  "table": null,
                                  "images": [],
                                  "importance": "4",
                                  "children": []
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**branches to abductor digiti minimi** (second branch)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**digital branch to fifth toe** (third branch)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "terminal branch",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**plantar branch** (see below)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial plantar arteries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "branches",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "terminal branch",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "anastomoses with the **first dorsal metatarsal branch of the dorsalis pedis artery**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**superficial digital branches join plantar metatarsal arteries of first three intermetatarsal spaces**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anterior Tibial Artery",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Origin the other, smaller, terminal branch of the popliteal artery",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/fig_6.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/origin_back_knee.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Course in leg",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**descends anterior to the interosseous membrane and supplies the muscles of the anterior compartment of the lower leg**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**it becomes superficial at the ankle midway between the malleoli**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**supplies muscles of the anterior compartement of the lower leg**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Branches at ankle",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**anterior medial malleolar artery**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**anterior lateral malleolar artery**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Branches in foot",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "dorsalis pedis artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**a continuation of the anterior tibial artery in the foot**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**palpable over the dorsum of the foot just lateral to the extensor hallicus longus tendon**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**branches**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**arcuate (see below)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**lateral tarsal**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**medial tarsal arteries**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "terminates at the first intermetatarsal space into",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**first dorsal metatarsal artery**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**deep plantar arch (see below)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Blood Supply to Distal Foot & Toes",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Plantar arch** origin",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "forms from the anastomosis of the lateral plantar artery and the dorsalis pedis artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "provides blood supply to plantar foot and toes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "branches",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "plantar digital arteries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "plantar metatarsal arteries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Arcuate artery**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/dorsalis_pedis_foot.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "is a vascular arch that runs in the dorsal midfoot deep to the extensor tendons",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**gives off dorsal metatarsal arteries that run in the 2nd, 3rd and 4th intermetatarsal spaces.**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Vein System of the Foot",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The **dorsal venous arch** drains into",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the **greater** and",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**lesser saphenous venous systems**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12114/images/fig_7.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
